<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 24 November, from 380 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodosius-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">380 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,646 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius I enters Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> made his formal entry into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Earlier that year he had declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicene-christianity">Nicene Christianity</a> the faith of the empire, and he soon removed the city's Arian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">847 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake strikes Damascus, Antioch and Mosul</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A powerful earthquake, perhaps part of a multiple event stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>, struck <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. There were an estimated 20,000 casualties in Antioch, according to the historian al-Dhahabi, and 50,000 in Mosul.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes">Antioch-on-the-Orontes</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1190">1190 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">836 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Conrad of Montferrat becomes King of Jerusalem by marriage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a>, who had held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, married Isabella I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and so became de facto King of Jerusalem. He was officially elected king only in April 1192, days before his murder.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1221">1221 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">805 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Genghis Khan defeats Jalal al-Din at the Battle of the Indus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus River</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> defeated Jalal al-Din, the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a>, who had rallied Khwarazmian loyalists after his father's flight and death. Jalal al-Din fought on in exile as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a> collapsed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasion-of-the-khwarazmian-empire">Mongol invasion of the Khwarazmian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1429">1429 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">597 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc lays siege to La Charité</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the orders of Charles VII, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> began a siege of La Charité, held since 1423 by the warlord Perrinet Gressard. The siege lasted until 25 December and failed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1859">1859 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Darwin publishes On the Origin of Species</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Murray published <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-darwin">Charles Darwin</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/on-the-origin-of-species">On the Origin of Species</a>, setting out evolution by natural selection. The first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> of 1,250 copies was quickly taken up, and the book transformed biology.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1922">1922 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">104 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Carter uncovers the sealed doorway of Tutankhamun's tomb</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With Lord Carnarvon present, Howard Carter's team cleared the stairway and found a sealed doorway bearing Tutankhamun's name. Two days later they looked inside.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jack Ruby shoots Lee Harvey Oswald on live television</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nightclub owner Jack Ruby shot Lee Harvey Oswald, accused of killing President Kennedy, in the basement of Dallas police headquarters. Millions saw the shooting live on television.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fossil hunters find 'Lucy' in Ethiopia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hadar, Donald Johanson and Tom Gray found the partial skeleton of a 3.2-million-year-old Australopithecus afarensis. Named Lucy, she showed that human ancestors walked upright long before brains enlarged.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 24 November <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philip-william-elector-palatine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philip-william-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philip William, Elector Palatine</span><span class="tp">1615–1690</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/baruch-spinoza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/baruch-spinoza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Baruch Spinoza</span><span class="tp">1632–1677</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/junipero-serra"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/junipero-serra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Junípero Serra</span><span class="tp">1713–1784</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oscar-carmona"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oscar-carmona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Óscar Carmona</span><span class="tp">1869–1951</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-burley-griffin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-burley-griffin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Burley Griffin</span><span class="tp">1876–1937</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 24 November <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leszek-the-white.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leszek the White</span><span class="tp">c. 1184–1227</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/magnus-olafsson"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Magnus Olafsson</span><span class="tp">d. 1265</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mingyi-nyo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mingyi-nyo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mingyi Nyo</span><span class="tp">1459–1530</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-knox"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-knox.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Knox</span><span class="tp">c. 1514–1572</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-brant"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-brant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph Brant</span><span class="tp">c. 1743–1807</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georges-clemenceau"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georges-clemenceau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georges Clemenceau</span><span class="tp">1841–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-rivera"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-rivera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Diego Rivera</span><span class="tp">1886–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-al-salim-al-sabah"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdullah-al-salim-al-sabah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abdullah Al-Salim Al-Sabah</span><span class="tp">1895–1965</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
